# The batch runner's own smoke test (docs/design/batch.md §11.4): every
# mechanism on the two small hosts in under an hour, at least two entries at
# once.  Done when it passes twice, its summary.tsv matches the runs' own
# reports, and each entry ran on the hosts `plan` predicted.
# No `set round`: t2 entries take the round at the fork heads (the backotter HEADs
# of ~/git/restic, rustic_core, rustic), built as t2r-... when none exists yet
# (testvm/test2/README.md).
# stic1 must name a round directory (drive.py): it stays pinned.
set hosts copland,cage

t2      GateTest2 selftest hosts=cage
t2      HoltTest2 alpine324
stic1   rel9 alpine324
cmd     true -- true
